\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee virtually pegged to US dollar -study  \b0\par\par\uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2005\par 11:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 5 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee, contrary to market perceptions, is virtually pegged to the U.S. dollar, according to a study presented by two economists on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) says it follows a "managed float" for the rupee <INR=IN>, implying that it guides the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of India's major trade partners.  \par \par \uc2 But an analysis from Tony Cavoli of the University of Adelaide and Ramkishen S. Rajan from Singapore's Lee Kuan Yew School of Public Policy suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  guides the rupee's exchange rate against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 In contrast, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) manages the Singapore dollar <SGD=> against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its top trade partners, the study found, confirming Singapore's official stance.  \par \par \uc2 "The Indian rupee appears to be a de facto U.S. dollar peg while the Singapore dollar is a genuine basket pegger," Cavoli said, presenting the paper at the Singapore Economic Review Conference.  \par \par \uc2 "The degree of influence of the U.S. dollar on the rupee is quite high."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials often cite the rupee's real effective exchange rate (REER) to indicate that the rupee is overvalued or undervalued against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its main trade partners.  \par \par \uc2 "The perception that RBI is targetting the REER is not right," said Rajan. "Since 1996, that's not true. That's not what we find."  \par \par \uc2 Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have a negligible influence on the rupee, he said, although the the euro <EUR=> is gradually gaining in importance.  \par \par \uc2 "The euro is becoming more important at the expense of the pound sterling <GBP=> and the yen," Cavoli said.  \par \par \uc2 For the Singapore dollar, the Japanese yen <JPY=> has been growing in influence since 1998, he said.  \par \par \uc2 The study also found that the degree of flexibility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements allowed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was lower than that allowed by the Reserve Bank of India.  \par \par \uc2 That means the degree of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  authority to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its preferred trading band is higher than that of the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Cavoli said. ((Reporting by Rajat Bhattacharya; editing by Alan Raybould; rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging: rajat.bhattacharya.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3841))  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-RUPEE|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|SI|SNI|SNS|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050805e185000ys\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
