\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down Late;Prospects Of Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2005\par 08:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was slightly weaker against its U.S. counterpart in Asia late Monday, weighed down by expectations of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Prices on government bonds were lower, in the wake of a fall in U.S. Treasury prices Friday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0635 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6611, up from S$1.6600 late Friday. It traded between S$1.6605 and S$1.6657 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the U.S. dollar's fall to as low as S$1.6605 on its weakness against the yen early in the session, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon found support above the psychologically important S$1.6600 level amid prospects of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  around that level to curb further appreciation of the local dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the MAS is perceived to be keen to temper any excessive rise of the Singapore dollar that may hurt growth in the city-state's export-reliant economy. The government is targeting growth of 2.5%-4.5% in 2005, down from 8.4% last year when the economy rebounded from a SARS outbreak in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar then consolidated steadily in the low-S$1.6600s for the rest of the session, as market players waited for the 1400 GMT release Monday of the U.S.'s Institute for Supply Management's manufacturing index in July.  \par \par \uc2 The median estimate of 15 economists surveyed Friday by Dow Jones Newswires and CNBC is for a reading of 54.0 for the ISM manufacturing index in July, compared with 53.8 in June.  \par \par \uc2 For this week, the U.S. dollar is likely to remain relatively supported versus the Singapore dollar as the yen could come under pressure ahead of Friday's vote by Japan's upper house on the privatization of the nation's postal system, United Overseas Bank said in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 "If unsuccessful, (Prime Minister Junichiro) Koizumi could decide to dissolve the parliament's lower house, which could put upward pressure on the USD/JPY," UOB said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       1.8125%    1.8125% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.03%      2.02% \par    10-year bond yield   2.67%      2.62% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.18%      2.14% \par    10-year swap offer   2.88%      2.82% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 70 BPs     68 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 01-08-05 0653GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050801e1810008v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
