\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Down Late; Profit-Taking On Yen Weakness  \b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2005\par 10:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell against its U.S. counterpart in Asia late Monday, as weakness in the Japanese yen led to unwinding of short positions in the U.S. unit that were built after China revalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds ended flat at the short end and slightly higher at the long end, helped by a recovery in U.S. Treasurys Friday.  \par \par \uc2 At 0755 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6649, up from S$1.6609 late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was lower at S$1.6597 at the start of trading in Singapore and slipped further to S$1.6585 in midday trade as players looked at gains in the Malaysian ringgit.  \par \par \uc2 But as the day progressed, banks sold the Singapore dollar due to weakness in the Japanese yen, said a trader.  \par \par \uc2 "When the market realized the Chinese yuan and the Malaysian ringgit weren't going anywhere for now they decided to offload short positions in the U.S. dollar," said a banker at a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 Fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  also kept players from pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar upward in early trade.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS last week said it will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar breaches its trade-weighted exchange rate band or if market conditions are too volatile.  \par \par \uc2 United Overseas Bank said in a research report that it expects the U.S. dollar to find strong resistance at S$1.6700. Therefore the bank maintains a bearish outlook for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the medium term.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       1.8750%    1.8750% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.01%      2.02% \par    10-year bond yield   2.66%      2.68% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.14%      2.16% \par    10-year swap offer   2.85%      2.88% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 71 BPs     72 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 25-07-05 0830GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050725e17p000h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
