\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Jump on yuan, central banks restrict gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Rajat Bhattacharya  \par \uc2 1,010 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 03:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 22 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped on Friday after China, bowing to years of international pressure, let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate, but dollar purchases by central banks and lack of a further rise in the yuan pared gains.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday China let the yuan <CNY=CFXS> appreciate by 2.1 percent to 8.11 per dollar, dropping the peg of 8.28 per dollar to adopt a system of valuing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket made up of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of major trading partners.  \par \par \uc2 "We think the biggest gainers will be the Japanese yen and Taiwan dollar, second will be Korean won, Singapore dollar and Indian rupee," DBS Bank economists Chua Hak Bin and Chris Leung, said in a report.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=KFTC> gained as much as 1.5 percent to a three-week high of 1,020.0 per dollar before closing local trading at 1,021.3.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose as much as 1.7 percent from late Asian trading on Thursday to 1.6516 per dollar before losing some ground to 1.6635 on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying. It hit a two-month high of 1.6490 in overnight trading.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> rose to a three-week high of 31.55 per dollar but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying helped cut gains. The Indian rupee <INR=IN> was the only Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that weakened on Friday. It lost more than half a percent from the previous day after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying pushed it from a six-year high of 43.115 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 YUAN OUTLOOK  \par \par \uc2 Traders said Asian authorities were likely to check gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  until China lets the yuan appreciate further.  \par \par \uc2 "The (Korean) government has clearly said they're going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time if there is a rapid change and if they find out the action is driven by speculators," said Lee Yoon Ho, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options trading manager at Shinhan Bank in Seoul.  \par \par \uc2 "The market participants see the yuan strengthening further because a 2 percent rise is not enough. But the problem is that the China government is not satisfied with that kind of expectation. We'll have to wait and watch the yuan rate in the next couple of days."  \par \par \uc2 Although the yuan will be allowed to rise or fall by 0.3 percent per day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  barely moved on Friday. The yuan opened local trading on Friday at 8.11 per dollar and weakened by 0.01 percent to close local trading at 8.1111.  \par \par \uc2 "Expectation for a bigger appreciation of the yuan's value was, and will be, unrealistic," the state-run China Daily said in an editorial.  \par \par \uc2 But investors betting on the yuan's future value using non-deliverable forward contracts <CNYNDF=> priced in as much as a 6.3 percent rise in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the next 12 months.  \par \par \uc2 "My intuition is that the market is in for a fight if they expect today's one-year forward contracts to mature in the money," Huw McKay, senior economist at Westpac Bank in Sydney said in a report.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR BOOST  \par \par \uc2 Claudio Piron, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JPMorgan Chase Bank, expects the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise by another 5 percent against the dollar by the end of 2005 and lift other regional units. Citigroup said it expected a further 3 percent gain by year-end.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar stood to gain the most initially "as it benefits from the potential double revaluation of the yuan and the ringgit", Piron said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 Malaysia dropped the ringgit's peg against the dollar on Thursday and moved to a system of managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The ringgit <MYR=> appreciated as much as 0.7 percent from its earlier peg of 3.8 per dollar to 3.7750 per dollar but dealers said dollar buying by the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it lower to 3.7790 in late Asian trading.  \par \par \uc2 JPMorgan said the ringgit was still undervalued by about 7 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) said on Friday it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  nears the top end of its undisclosed policy band but reiterated its aim for a gradual and modest appreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Despite MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Piron expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to advance further, along with the South Korean won and the Taiwan dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Appreciation pressure on the Singapore dollar could also be exacerbated for lack of other alternatives in Southeast Asia as the Philippine peso, Thai baht and Indonesian rupiah are beset with either political woes, trade deficits or dollar-oil demand," Piron said. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0815 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.82         112.36       +1.39\par  China yuan      8.1111         8.1100       -0.014\par  Sing dlr        1.6608         1.6804       +1.18\par  Taiwan dlr      31.635         31.953       +1.01\par  Korean won     1020.80        1035.50       +1.44\par  Ringgit         3.7790         3.8000       +0.56\par  Baht             41.35          41.90       +1.33\par  Peso             55.85          55.77       -0.14\par  Rupiah         9760.00        9816.00       +0.57\par  Rupee            43.44          43.19       -0.56 Change on\par year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.82         102.45       -7.55\par  China yuan      8.1111         8.2800       +2.082\par  Sing dlr        1.6608         1.6310       -1.79\par  Taiwan dlr      31.635         31.920       +0.90\par  Korean won     1020.80        1035.10       +1.40\par  Ringgit         3.7790         3.8000       +0.56\par  Baht             41.35          38.88       -5.97\par  Peso             55.85          56.28       +0.77\par  Rupiah         9760.00        9290.00       -4.82\par  Rupee            43.44          43.47       +0.08\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|Z|IF|PHD|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050722e17m000qr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
