\par\par \b \uc2 USD/SGD At 1.6578 Vs 1.6565 As MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 -Dealers  \b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 02:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar came back from early Friday morning highs after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6578 after the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , recovering from its early lows around S$1.6565.  \par \par \uc2 "They seem to have come in," said a trader at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 The suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after the MAS said late Thursday the move by China to revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't have a major impact on the Singapore dollar or the MAS exchange rate system.  \par \par \uc2 "Our current exchange rate policy stance remains appropriate. The fundamentals of the economy have not changed, nor have the factors influencing the growth prospects for the Singapore economy," MAS said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 MAS will continue to maintain the current policy of a modest and gradual appreciation of the Singapore dollar against a trade weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires;  \par \par \uc2 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com [ 22-07-05 0024GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--In the wake of China's revaluation of the yuan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore reiterated Friday that its Singapore dollar policy stance of modest and gradual appreciation remains appropriate.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual review, Deputy Managing Director Ong Chong Tee said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar breaches its trade weighted exchange rate band.  \par \par \uc2 "We will only come in when the trade weighted index has breached its policy band and if market conditions are volatile," he said. [ 22-07-05 0406GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Ong said the local dollar is currently in the "upper half of the band."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He wouldn't confirm if MAS had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market since last night to tackle excessive gains in the Singapore dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6630 at 0445 GMT, recovering from an early low of S$1.6511 on suspected MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar had rallied by more than 1.7% before shedding some of its gains against the U.S. dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MAS doesn't disclose its policy band, but United Overseas Bank in a research report Friday said assuming 2% on each side of the midpoint, the band is currently S$1.6878 to S$1.6548 with the midpoint at S$1.6217.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ong said the MAS is comfortable with its current policy band.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Heng Kwee Keat, managing director of MAS, said moves by China and Malaysia to reform their exchange rate system are a positive development for Asia.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It just gives us (Asia) better buffer to absorb shocks in the future," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When asked if the monetary authorities were looking at movements in the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the change in its regime, he said the MAS is monitoring the situation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But he noted the statement by Malaysian officials that the ringgit won't deviate too much from the value it had when it was pegged to the U.S. dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Malaysian ringgit gained only 0.4% by midday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the economy, Heng said the outlook for Singapore remains positive because electronics sector demand will improve in the second half of the year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Our assessment is that we will see a pickup in IT in the second half which will help the Singapore economy," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The latest data from the U.S. and the Chinese economy have also reinforced the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's view that the second half will be better for the local economy, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Heng said MAS expects Singapore's economy will grow between 2.5% to 4.5% in 2005, reiterating a government forecast for economic growth.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said the current monetary policy stance remains appropriate and the next policy statement will be released in October.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Heng said MAS remains vigilant against inflation despite headline inflation being low in the first half.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The economy is close to its potential output level and there are upside risks to the external inflation environment including, from the persistently high oil prices," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar and Kevin Lim, Dow Jones Newswires;  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Stephen Wright [ 22-07-05 0503GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050722e17m00009\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
