\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore MAS: SGD Policy Stance Remains Appropriate -2-  \b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2005\par 08:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Ong said the local dollar is currently in the 'upper half of the band.'  \par \par \uc2 He wouldn't confirm if MAS had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since last night to tackle excessive gains in the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6630 at 0445 GMT, recovering from an early low of S$1.6511 on suspected MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar had rallied by more than 1.7% before shedding some of its gains against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 MAS doesn't disclose its policy band, but United Overseas Bank in a research report Friday said assuming 2% on each side of the midpoint, the band is currently S$1.6878 to S$1.6548 with the midpoint at S$1.6217.  \par \par \uc2 Ong said the MAS is comfortable with its current policy band.  \par \par \uc2 Heng Kwee Keat, managing director of MAS, said moves by China and Malaysia to reform their exchange rate system are a positive development for Asia.  \par \par \uc2 'It just gives us (Asia) better buffer to absorb shocks in the future,' he said.  \par \par \uc2 When asked if the monetary authorities were looking at movements in the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the change in its regime, he said the MAS is monitoring the situation.  \par \par \uc2 But he noted the statement by Malaysian officials that the ringgit won't deviate too much from the value it had when it was pegged to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit gained only 0.4% by midday.  \par \par \uc2 On the economy, Heng said the outlook for Singapore remains positive because electronics sector demand will improve in the second half of the year.  \par \par \uc2 'Our assessment is that we will see a pickup in IT in the second half which will help the Singapore economy,' he said.  \par \par \uc2 The latest data from the U.S. and the Chinese economy have also reinforced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's view that the second half will be better for the local economy, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Heng said MAS expects Singapore's economy will grow between 2.5% to 4.5% in 2005, reiterating a government forecast for economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 He said the current monetary policy stance remains appropriate and the next policy statement will be released in October.  \par \par \uc2 Heng said MAS remains vigilant against inflation despite headline inflation being low in the first half.  \par \par \uc2 'The economy is close to its potential output level and there are upside risks to the external inflation environment including, from the persistently high oil prices,' he said. -By Saeed Azhar and Kevin Lim, Dow Jones Newswires;  \par \par \uc2 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Stephen Wright  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050722e17m004bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
