\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Down Late; Near 9-Month Low On Yen Fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2005\par 10:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell to nearly a nine-month low against the U.S. dollar in late Asian trade Friday, dragged down by a surge of the U.S. unit against the Japanese yen following a rate hike by the Federal Reserve.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond prices rose slightly after overnight gains in U.S. Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit traded between S$1.6823 and S$1.6908, its highest level since S$1.6906 on Oct. 8. At 0722 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6894, up from S$1.6820 late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "Although there's a long weekend in the U.S., the market went a bit wild after the Japanese yen fell," said a dealer at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they were expecting some consolidation Friday ahead of the weekend and the July 4 holiday in the U.S. However, selling in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  accelerated after the U.S. dollar rose to a near-nine-month high of Y111.13.  \par \par \uc2 Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are at multi-month lows against the U.S. dollar due to high oil prices, weakening speculation of a yuan revaluation, and rising U.S. interest rates. The Federal Reserve, as expected, on Thursday raised its key target rate to 3.25% from 3%.  \par \par \uc2 United Overseas Bank said in a research report the U.S. dollar should face resistance above S$1.6900 because market players will be cautious of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Singapore dollar has support because the MAS doesn't appear to be in the mood of abandoning its policy of modest and gradual appreciation of the local dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the next few months, UOB said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       1.813%     2.063% \par    Two-year bond yield  1.94%      1.95% \par    10-year bond yield   2.61%      2.62% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.11%      2.13% \par    10-year swap offer   2.73%      2.78% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 62 BPs     65 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 01-07-05 0830GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050701e171000bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
