\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Up Late On Yen Gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2005\par 09:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose against the U.S. dollar late Thursday, gaining back some of the ground it lost Wednesday as it tracked the recovering Japanese yen.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond prices fell across the curve, but a bigger upward move at the short-end yield on firmer overnight rates, slightly flattened the yield curve.  \par \par \uc2 At 0630 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6820, up from S$1.6847 late Wednesday. It traded between S$1.6819 and S$1.6870.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar failed to stay above the S$1.6850 resistance level, which prompted banks to cut positions, said a trader.  \par \par \uc2 There was also talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  above S$1.6850, making players cautious, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Despite Thursday's recovery most technical analysts are still suggesting a bearish trend for the Singapore dollar. The local unit suffered a blow recently after weaker-than-expected manufacturing and export data for May.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar's outlook has turned bullish in the medium-term after its global rally in past few days, said the United Overseas Bank in a report Thursday. It recommends buying the U.S. unit at S$1.6820, with the next target at S$1.6980. It recommends selling the U.S. dollar if it weakens below S$1.6720.  \par \par \uc2 BNP Paribas said a move above S$1.6800 opens further upside potential for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , allowing it to test S$1.700.  \par \par \uc2 "A break of a major downtrend line at S$1.6825 hints of a new trend in motion which is a bullish U.S. dollar," it said in a report.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       2.063%     1.813% \par    Two-year bond yield  1.99%      1.94% \par    10-year bond yield   2.66%      2.63% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.13%      2.13% \par    10-year swap offer   2.78%      2.76% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 65 BPs     63 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Costas Paris [ 30-06-05 0719GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050630e16u000ae\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
