\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dollar Up Late, Rebounds From Key Support   \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 2005\par 08:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose modestly against its U.S. counterpart in Asia late Friday, rebounding from a key support level while tracking range-bound trade in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Government bonds were flat at the short end, but the 10-year yield rose fractionally in lackluster trading, snapping alonger-end rally in the past two weeks, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 At 0605 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6587, down from S$1.6617 late Thursday. It traded between S$1.6574 and S$1.6608 intraday.   \par \par \uc2 A trader said the U.S. dollar met resistance around S$1.6000 amid fears since Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a bigger weakness in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar, meanwhile, rallied against the euro in anticipation of a likely rejection of a referendum vote on the European Union in France over the weekend.   \par \par \uc2 'Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were generally range-bound, which also kept the Singapore dollar in a tight range,' the trader said. Trading volume was also thin ahead of a three-day weekend in the U.S. and the U.K.   \par \par \uc2 Technical analysis suggests U.S.-dollar bullishness in the medium term. The tone will be neutralized only if the U.S. unit weakens below S$1.6510, United Overseas Bank said in a research report.   \par \par \uc2 The following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       2.00%      1.9375% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.02%      2.02% \par    10-year bond yield   2.68%      2.67% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.20%      2.17% \par    10-year swap offer   2.88%      2.88% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 68 BPs     71 BPs \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par      \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg  }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com -Edited by Ven Ram -0-    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050527e15r0040h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
