\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Steady Late On Threat Of  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2005\par 09:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was relatively steady against its U.S. counterpart in Asia late Wednesday, as the threat of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept a lid on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside.  \par \par \uc2 Prices on government bonds edged up, tracking slightly higher U.S. Treasurys prices late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 At 0650 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6547, nearly unchanged from S$1.6550 late Tuesday. It traded between S$1.6527 and S$1.6564 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 Early in the session, speculators used a media report that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore had reaffirmed its current stance of gradual and modest appreciation of the Singapore dollar as an excuse to push the U.S. dollar down as low as S$1.6527, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reported remarks came on the heels of the International Monetary Fund's economic survey released Monday, in which the IMF recommended that Singapore may need to change its current tight monetary policy to a supportive one if its economic slowdown worsens. Since April 2004, the MAS has maintained a tight policy that allows a 'modest and gradual appreciation' of the Singapore dollar to counter inflationary pressures.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon rebounded to the mid-S$1.6500s on speculation that the MAS had checked the prevailing U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar exchange rates with Singapore-based banks, a move that was widely interpreted as a prelude to potential \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit then consolidated in the mid-S$1.6500s for the rest of the session, ahead of the 1230 GMT release of the U.S. durable goods orders data for April. The median estimate of 21 economists surveyed Monday by Dow Jones Newswires and CNBC is for a 1.5% increase in new orders for durable goods.  \par \par \uc2 In the short term, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to dip, then rise again to test immediate resistance at S$1.6610, based on technical analysis, said United Overseas Bank in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 'As long as the critical support at S$1.6510 is not taken out, the probability of a resumption of the recent (U.S. dollar) up-move is still good,' UOB said.  \par \par \uc2 As a short-term trading strategy, UOB recommended buying the U.S. unit at S$1.6540 and placing stop-loss sales orders below S$1.6510 in anticipation of a potential rise to S$1.6620.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       1.7500%    1.7500% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.00%      2.02% \par    10-year bond yield   2.71%      2.74% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.18%      2.18% \par    10-year swap offer   2.92%      2.97% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 74 BPs     79 BPs \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com -Edited by Mary de Wet -0