\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late On HKMA Move, But Off Early Highs  \b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2005\par 08:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose against its U.S. counterpart in Asia late Thursday, as a move by Hong Kong to tweak its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg fanned speculation that China may revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon.  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar shed some early gains amid suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. The MAS didn't comment on the matter.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds extended gains along the curve, after subdued U.S. inflation data overnight pushed up U.S. Treasurys, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0632 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6543, down from S$1.6580 late Wednesday.The U.S. unit fell to as low as S$1.6496 during the session before recovering on suspected MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It traded between S$1.6496 and S$1.6554 intraday. "The MAS was proactive in preventing speculators from using the Singapore dollar as a proxy to a (possible) yuan revaluation," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that it would introduce a ceiling for the Hong Kong dollar against the U.S. dollar to discourage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from being used as a trading proxy for speculation about a revaluation of the Chinese yuan.  \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's action only served to increase speculation that China would soon change its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, allowing the yuan to appreciate against the U.S. dollar, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Technical analysis suggests, however, that there is no change to the medium-term bullish view for the U.S. dollar versus the Singapore dollar unless the pair breaks S$1.6450, United Overseas Bank said in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 "The outlook will shift to neutral only upon a move below the strong support at S$1.6450. The price action over the next couple of days should be able to indicate whether the bullish view is tenable," the report said.  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields fell across the curve, and the yield curve flattened reacting to gains in U.S. Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year yield fell by four basis points to 2.83%, a level last seen May 6, while the two-year bond yield dropped three basis points to 2.05%  \par \par \uc2 The following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       1.7500%    1.6250% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.05%      2.08% \par    10-year bond yield   2.83%      2.87% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.23%      2.24% \par    10-year swap offer   3.06%      3.09% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 83 BPs     85 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 19-05-05 0658GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050519e15j000az\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\pi