\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dlr Up Late On HKMA Move, But Off Early Highs  \b0\par\par\uc2 485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2005\par 09:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose against its U.S. counterpart in Asia late Thursday, as a move by Hong Kong to tweak its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg fanned speculation that China may revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon.  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar shed some early gains amid suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. The MAS didn't comment on the matter.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds extended gains along the curve, after subdued U.S. inflation data overnight pushed up U.S. Treasurys, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   At 0632 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6543, down from S$1.6580 late Wednesday.The U.S. unit fell to as low as S$1.6496 during the session before recovering on suspected MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  It traded between S$1.6496 and S$1.6554 intraday.   'The MAS was proactive in preventing speculators from using the Singapore dollar as a proxy to a (possible) yuan revaluation,' said a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader. \par   Wednesday, the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said that it would introduce a ceiling for the Hong Kong dollar against the U.S. dollar to discourage the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from being used as a trading proxy for speculation about a revaluation of the Chinese yuan. \par   Hong Kong's action only served to increase speculation that China would soon change its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg, allowing the yuan to appreciate against the U.S. dollar, analysts said. \par   Technical analysis suggests, however, that there is no change to the medium-term bullish view for the U.S. dollar versus the Singapore dollar unless the pair breaks S$1.6450, United Overseas Bank said in a research report. \par   'The outlook will shift to neutral only upon a move below the strong support at S$1.6450. The price action over the next couple of days should be able to indicate whether the bullish view is tenable,' the report said. \par   In the bond market, yields fell across the curve, and the yield curve flattened reacting to gains in U.S. Treasurys. \par   The 10-year yield fell by four basis points to 2.83%, a level last seen May 6, while the two-year bond yield dropped three basis points to 2.05% \par   The following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps. \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       1.7500%    1.6250% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.05%      2.08% \par    10-year bond yield   2.83%      2.87% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.23%      2.24% \par    10-year swap offer   3.06%      3.09% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 83 BPs     85 BPs \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com -Edited by Ven Ram -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050519e15j004xt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
