\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Down Late On Talk Of MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2005\par 09:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar fell against its U.S. counterpart late Friday in Asia amid talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second day to ward off speculative upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Yields on Singapore government bonds rose, tracking overnight losses in U.S. Treasury markets, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0700 GMT, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at S$1.6506, up from S$1.6481 late Thursday. It traded between S$1.6475 and S$1.6513 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced local banks to step up buying of the U.S. dollar, lifting it above a resistance level of S$1.6500. The MAS didn't comment on the rumor.  \par \par \uc2 "There's been talk in the market about MAS trying to ward off any hot money flows," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader.  \par \par \uc2 He cited ongoing speculation about a revaluation of the Chinese yuan as putting upward pressure on the Singapore dollar, which gathered momentum after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's overnight comment calling on China to move to a flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime.  \par \par \uc2 United Overseas Bank said in a research report Friday that the MAS appears to be trying to discourage the market from using the Singapore dollar as a proxy tool for any change in the Malaysian ringgit or the Chinese yuan.  \par \par \uc2 "Indeed the authorities appear keen to keep the SGD NEER around the midpoint of the SGD policy band, currently 0.012% stronger than the midpoint," the report said.  \par \par \uc2 It expects the U.S. dollar to find strong support at S$1.6450 and resistance at S$1.6535.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar's movement was also in a different direction from the Japanese yen which it normally tracks closely. The dollar fell slightly against the yen in Asia Friday, as traders bought the yen following Greenspan's yuan comments.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       1.937%     2.000%% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.12%      2.10% \par    10-year bond yield   2.98%      2.96% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.33%      2.30% \par    10-year swap offer   3.20%      3.19% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 87 BPs     89 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 22-04-05 0737GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050422e14m000a0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
