\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Steady Late After Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2005\par 09:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was relatively steady against its U.S. counterpart late Thursday in Asia after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  government bonds rose in the short end but fell in the long end, leading to the curve flattening, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0630 GMT, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at S$1.6481, nearly unchanged from S$1.6485 late Wednesday. It traded between S$1.6455 and S$1.6495 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 After opening near its intraday low of S$1.6455, the U.S. dollar surged to as high as S$1.6495 early in the session, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit a further rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness against its major rivals throughout the session and ongoing worries over U.S. economic growth weighed down the U.S. dollar against its Singaporean counterpart in the afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 Looming event risks later in the global session, such as the 1230 GMT release of U.S. initial jobless claims and the 1400 GMT speech by Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland President Sandra Pianalto on the 'Power of Price Stability,' kept market participants mostly sidelined.  \par \par \uc2 From a technical analysis perspective, there is no sign of stabilization for the U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar pair yet and a further decline in the U.S. unit is likely, despite oversold conditions, said United Overseas Bank in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 'As the downward momentum is not very strong, (we) expect any down-move to be slow and grinding,' UOB said. 'On the upside, only a move above S$1.6530 will suggest that a recovery is on the way.'  \par \par \uc2 As a short-term trading strategy, UOB recommended selling the U.S. unit at S$1.6500 and placing stop-loss orders above S$1.6530, in anticipation of a possible fall to S$1.6430.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       2.0000%    2.1250% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.10%      2.08% \par    10-year bond yield   2.96%      2.98% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.30%      2.28% \par    10-year swap offer   3.19%      3.17% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 89 BPs     89 BPs \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com -Edited by Paul Baylis -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050421e14l005eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
