\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down Late;Rumored MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ,Yen Fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2005\par 08:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar fell significantly against its U.S. counterpart late Friday in Asia, dragged down by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the weakness of the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on Singapore government bonds rose in the front end, but were flat to lower in the medium- to long-term sectors, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0645 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6600, up sharply from S$1.6510 late Thursday. It traded between S$1.6548 and S$1.6618 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 Early in the session, Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy the U.S. dollar around the S$1.6570 level, sparking short-covering that eventually lifted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as high as S$1.6618 in the afternoon, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been aimed at scaring away speculators from betting on a sharp rise in the Singapore dollar against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming sessions after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided earlier this week to retain its current policy of modest and gradual appreciation of the Singapore dollar, dealers added.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's weakness against the U.S. and most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the session also helped weigh down the Singapore dollar. At 0645 GMT, the U.S. unit was at Y108.28, up from Y108.11 late Thursday in New York.  \par \par \uc2 But, with both the two-day meeting of the finance ministers and central bankers of the Group of Seven leading industrial nations and the Treasury International Capital flows data looming later in the global session, market participants refrained from pushing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply higher against the local dollar.  \par \par \uc2 According to technical analysis, the U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar's medium-term outlook is still neutral, said United Overseas Bank in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 "Critical resistance is at S$1.6700 and unless this level is taken out, we are probably caught in a wide sideways consolidation," UOB said.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on short-dated Singapore government bonds rose slightly on tightening liquidity conditions in the money market, as reflected by the rise in the overnight interbank rate to 1.9375% Friday from 1.8750% Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Longer-dated local government bond yields, however, were flat to lower, given Thursday's strength in U.S. Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       1.9375%    1.8750% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.10%      2.09% \par    10-year bond yield   3.05%      3.09% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.32%      2.34% \par    10-year swap offer   3.26%      3.32% \par    2-10-yr swap spread:  94 BPs     98 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http:/