\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Down Vs US Dlr Late On Weak Yen, MAS-Talk  \b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2005\par 10:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell against the U.S. unit late Friday after testing a seven-week low in early trade, dragged down by a weaker yen and speculative selling ahead of a policy review by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds were higher, with the 10-year bond edging up in line with the rise in U.S. treasurys late Thursday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0755 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6554, up from S$1.6504 late Thursday. It rose to a seven-week high of S$1.6588 before surrendering a part of its gains on profit-taking. It traded between S$1.6500 and S$1.6588 in intraday trade.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said rumors that the MAS may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar ahead of a policy review April 12 also caused early jitters in the market.  \par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for the MAS said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which provided some relief to market participants.  \par \par \uc2 Most analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain its policy of a modest and gradual appreciation of the Singapore dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its trading partners.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer at a foreign bank said some speculators may test the MAS' resolve ahead of the semiannual policy review.  \par \par \uc2 Thomas Loong, a treasury economist at United Overseas Bank, said the sharp intraday movement in the pair was due to the yen's weakness and the breach of the S$1.6550 barrier early in the session, which triggered some stop-losses for the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 A worse-than-expected "tankan" quarterly business sentiment survey issued by the Bank of Japan sent the yen sliding to a five-week low.  \par \par \uc2 The financial markets now await the issue of U.S. non-farm payrolls data Friday. If data show that the world's largest economy added more than 250,000 new jobs in March, the greenback's rise against the yen will gain pace, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers say.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds rose, with the 10-year bond yield fell to 3.11% from 3.14%.  \par \par \uc2 The following are yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest     Previous \par .Overnight rate       1.938%     1.875% \par .Two-year bond yield  2.07%      2.09% \par .10-year bond yield   3.11%      3.14% \par .Two-year swap offer  2.40%      2.43% \par .10-year swap offer   3.35%      3.39% \par .2-10-yr swap spread: 95 BPs     96 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 01-04-05 0826GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050401e141000dn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
