\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing, Taiwan dlr weaken on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 709 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , March 11 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar led\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower on Friday on worries central banks may\par again step in after some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a day earlier to pull their\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from multi-year highs to keep exports competitive.\par  \par     The Singapore dollar, which touched a 6-1/2-year high on\par Thursday, fell 0.2 percent to 1.6212 per dollar.\par     The Taiwan dollar, Asia's second-best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar this year, slipped a tenth of a percent to\par 30.820 per dollar, easing from a 4-1/2-year high on Thursday.\par     Analysts said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, which\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 guides the trade-weighted Singapore dollar within an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 undisclosed band, may no longer want a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 because of the dim outlook for electronics and bio-medical  \par \par \uc2 exports. MAS has maintained a bias towards appreciation since  \par \par \uc2 last year.  \par \par \uc2 "There may be a chance that the MAS may shift to a neutral  \par \par \uc2 policy come April," said Emmanuel Ng, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \par \par \uc2 ABN AMRO Bank in Singapore, referring to the next MAS policy  \par \par \uc2 meeting.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The Singapore dollar's nominal effective exchange rate has\par been kept on a tight leash in the year to date."\par     Ng said inflation may not be a major cause for concern for\par MAS because the effects of high oil prices are likely to be\par limited. That weakens the argument for a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     South Korea made it clear it was uncomfortable with the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 won's rise, which has made South Korean exporters less  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 competitive against regional rivals. The won has surged 10  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent against the yen since the start of November and touched  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a 5-1/2-year high of 9.52 per yen on Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won weakened to 9.6 per yen on Friday after South  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea's deputy finance minister, Bahk Byong-won, said the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government would not stay idle in the face of rapid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 movements, which he said were driven by speculation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Given that backdrop, ABN AMRO expected the won to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strengthen only 1 percent in the next three months to about 990  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the dollar, despite a revival in domestic consumer  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 demand.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan Chase Bank said in a report that although South  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea does not want a sharp weakening of the dollar, it may not  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stand in the way of any longer-term weakness.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The monetary authorities will unlikely attempt to turn  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 broader market trends (dollar weakness) and should gradually  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 cede local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation," JPMorgan said in a note to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 clients.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concern about the dollar's long-term decline was fuelled on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday when India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, Yaga Venugopal  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reddy, said diversification of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 being discussed within the bank and that it was a subject of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ongoing debate among all central banks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee was steady at 43.58 per dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso, Asia's best performer this year, was the only  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian unit to gain on Friday, rising a quarter of a percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ng said the peso was benefitting from foreign investment in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stocks, remittances from overseas Filipinos and expectations of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 foreign direct investment in its mining and power industries.   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at   0802 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.09         103.87       -0.21\par  Sing dlr        1.6212         1.6184       -0.17\par  Taiwan dlr      30.820         30.790       -0.10\par  Korean won     1000.20        1000.10       -0.01\par  Baht             38.28          38.27       -0.03\par  Peso             54.13          54.25       +0.22\par  Rupiah         9360.00        9352.00       -0.09\par  Rupee            43.58          43.58       -0.02 Change on\par year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.09         102.45       -1.5