\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr, won weaken on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 04:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , March 11 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar led\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower on Friday on worries central banks may\par again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  competitive after they\par had pulled Asian units down from multi-year highs a day\par earlier.\par     The Singapore dollar, which touched a 6-1/2-year high on\par Thursday, fell 0.3 percent to 1.6230 per dollar. The South\par Korean won edged down to 1,002 per dollar, extending its\par retreat a seven-year high of 989 on Thursday.\par     Analysts said South Korea, which was estimated to have\par spent $2 billion on Thursday to block the won's strength, may\par spend more in buying dollars to keep the country's exporters\par competitive, particularly against Japan.\par     The South Korean unit has surged almost 10 percent against\par the yen since the start of November, to reach its strongest\par level since and mid-1999.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Until we get concrete evidence that the domestic\par consumption recovery is firmly entrenched, we believe the 9.50\par level for the yen-won will provide good support," said Emmanuel\par Ng, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at ABN AMRO Bank in Singapore.\par     South Korean deputy finance minister Bahk Byong-won said\par the government would not stay idle in the face of rapid\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements, which he said were driven by speculation.\par     Given that backdrop, ABN AMRO expected the won to\par strengthen only 1 percent in the next three months to about 990\par per dollar, despite a revival in domestic consumer demand.\par     The Taiwan dollar, Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar this year after the Philippine peso , also\par slipped a tenth of a percent on worries the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for a second day.\par  \par     Foreign investors, who have buoyed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year,\par turned net sellers on Thursday for the second time this month.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also been weighed by a bill being debated\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in China's parliament that would authorise China to use force  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to prevent Taiwan from seceding from the mainland. Traders were  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 waiting on Taiwan's response to the bill.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupiah, Asia's worst performer after the Japanese yen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this year, remained pressured by dollar demand from importers  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and near-record oil prices, which analysts say could worsen the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 country's balance of payments position.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso was the only Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday morning, on expectations authorities would allow gains  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to help counter inflation pressures from high oil prices.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ng said the peso continued to benefit from foreign  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investments in stocks, strong remittances from Filipinos living  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 abroad and expectations of foreign direct investments into its  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mining and power industries.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Manila's key stock index hit a 5-1/2-year high this week.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at   0241 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.11         103.87       -0.23\par  Sing dlr        1.6229         1.6184       -0.28\par  Taiwan dlr      30.813         30.790       -0.07\par  Korean won     1000.70        1000.10       -0.06\par  Baht             38.32          38.27       -0.13\par  Peso             54.22          54.25       +0.06\par  Rupiah         9360.00        9352.00       -0.09\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.11         102.45       -1.59\par  Sing dlr        1.6229         1.6310       +0.50\par  Taiwan dlr      30.813         31.920       +3.59\par  Korean won     1000.70        1035.10       +3.44\par  Baht             38.32          38.88       +1.46\par  Peso             54.22          56.28       +3.80\par  Rupiah         9360.00        9290.00       -0.75\par  Rupee            43.58          43.47       -0.24 ((Editing by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 John Mair; rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rajat.bhattacharya.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3841)).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050311e13b0015r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
