\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Knocked from multi-year highs by c.banks.  \b0\par\par\uc2 907 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 09:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, March 10 (Reuters) - The South Korean won,\par Taiwan dollar and the Singapore dollar were knocked off\par multi-year highs on Thursday when some Asian central banks\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthening and keep\par exports competitive.\par     The South Korean won ended local trading at 1,000.3 per\par dollar, barely changed from the previous day's close of 1,001\par but off a seven-year high of 989 hit in the morning.\par  \par     Traders said the government bought almost $2 billion in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to pull the won off its highs.\par     "That's definitely a step up (in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) from what\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 we've seen in recent times but they haven't got a lot of bang  \f28 \par \par \uc2 for it," said David Simmonds, emerging markets strategist at  \par \par \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland's \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  office.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts may be quite persistent from here\par on for a while. Some of the fast money has already been made."\par     The Taiwan dollar ended local trading 0.1 percent stronger\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at 30.79 per dollar. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yielded ground after hitting  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a 4-1/2-year high of 30.67 following dollar buying  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar hit a 6-1/2-year high of about 1.6162 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar before softening, while the yen gained 0.7 percent from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 late Asian trading on Wednesday to trade at about 103.87 per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains were triggered by South Korean\par data which showed consumer sentiment hit a two-year high.\par     Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi fueled the rally\par further by telling a parliament committee that it was necessary\par for Japan to diversify its record foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves.\par     Japan had until now refrained from echoing other Asian\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 policy makers who have publicly announced plans to diversify  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 their holdings away from dollar-denominated assets. Asian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 central banks hold about $2.5 trillion of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 reserves.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DAMAGE CONTROL  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soared, Japanese finance ministry  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 officials said Japan had no plans to change the composition of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the country's $840.56 billion reserves, the world's largest.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     South Korean finance ministry and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials\par joined in the damage control.\par     Bank of Korea Governor Park Seung called for "international\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 action" to counter the dollar's weakness and promised  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 aggressive steps to check the gains in the won, which he said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was excessively strong.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won has gained 3.5 percent this year, making it Asia's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the Taiwan dollar which has  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strengthened 3.7 percent. The won gained 15.2 percent in 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The won and the Taiwan dollar have been our top picks (in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia) for the last six months and there's no reason to change  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that now," said James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Deutsche  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank in Singapore.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Investor interest is shifting back to Asia because other  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economies are not looking that attractive. This is the region  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 where the growth will be the strongest, this is the region  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are undervalued."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malcolm said speculators who had been on the sidelines  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 since the start of the year after bidding up Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 in the last quarter of 2004 were once again buying them.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although the U.S. economy is on a rebound, investors are  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 revisiting the longer-term problems facing the dollar such as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the bloated U.S. current account deficit, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With investors in north Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  facing  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders bid up the Philippine peso and Indonesian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rupiah on expectations their central banks would not mind  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as they battle inflationary pressures from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 near-record high oil prices.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine peso gained as much as half a percent to set a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fresh 19-month high of 54.15 per dollar. The country has  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 benefitted from strong inflows into its stock market, which  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 drove the benchmark stock index to a 5-1/2-year high this week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Simmonds said further moves in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 depend on oil prices, terms of trade of each country and equity  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 inflows. But he ruled out any joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Asian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "I'd be very surprised if there's any sort of coordinated\par efforts," he said. "At best these are smoothening-off efforts."\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at   0802 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.87         104.58       +0.68\par  Sing dlr        1.6184         1.6200       +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      30.786         30.819       +0.11\par  Korean won     1000.10        1001.00       +0.09\par  Baht             38.27          38.29       +0.07\par  Peso             54.25          54.41       +0.29\par  Rupiah         9352.00        9385.00       +0.35\par  Rupee            43.54          43.62       +0.20\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highli