\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late Hit By Early Yen Rally, Bonds Rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 08:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose against its U.S. counterpart late Thursday in Asia after a Japanese yen rally, but retreated from a new six-year high due to suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds rose, with the longer-dated 10-year yield hitting a five-month high, reacting to the second day of a selloff in U.S. Treasurys overnight.  \par \par \uc2 At 0640 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6189, down from S$1.6214 late Wednesday. It traded between S$1.6161 and S$1.6206 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar - which closely tracks the yen - rose sharply against the U.S. dollar early in the session after a rally in the yen following Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's remarks that diversity in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves was necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Soon after, however, an official at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Dow Jones Newswires that Tokyo has no intention of shifting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makeup of its reserves, and that the prime minister was likely referring to diversification within Japan's dollar-denominated assets.  \par \par \uc2 After sliding to a new six-year low of S$1.6161 in early trade, the U.S. dollar then rebounded to the S$1.6189 area later in the session as calm returned to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 "Koizumi's comments had a big impact on the market, but after the clarification, the pressure on the U.S. dollar eased a bit," said a Singapore dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downside against its Singaporean counterpart was also supported by rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the MAS, with some dealers saying the U.S. unit could find strong support at S$1.6150.  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, the 10-year yield rose to 3.24%, a five-month high, after Wednesday's strong selling in the U.S. Treasurys market that sent the 10-year Treasury yield above 4.50% for the first time since July.  \par \par \uc2 Following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest       Previous \par Overnight rate       1.6875%      1.6875% \par Two-year bond yield  2.06%        2.04% \par 10-year bond yield   3.24%        3.18% \par Two-year swap offer  2.36%        2.34% \par 10-year swap offer   3.49%        3.44% \par 2-10-yr swap spread  113 Bps      110 Bps \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; (65) 6415-4150; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 10-03-05 0722GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050310e13a000g3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
