\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Bonds Tumble On Treasurys, Tight MAS Policy  \b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 05:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--A sharp fall in U.S. Treasurys sparked fresh selling at the longer end of Singapore's bond market Thursday, driving the benchmark 10-year bond yield to a five-month high.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year bond opened at a yield of 3.22% and rose to 3.24% by 0400 GMT, up from 3.18% Wednesday. The market reacted to selling in the U.S., where Treasurys sank to new session lows overnight, sending the 10-year U.S. yield above 4.50% for the first time since July.  \par \par \uc2 The selling shows the city-state is facing a double-edged sword - the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore has been on a tightening trend since October to contain inflation, while yields on the U.S. Treasurys are moving higher at a faster pace.  \par \par \uc2 In order to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar competitive, the MAS has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent a sharp fall in the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Even on Thursday, suspected MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the U.S. dollar to rebound from a new six-year low of 1.6160 in early trade. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment.  \par \par \uc2 However, at the same time, MAS is also sterilizing surplus liquidity through the sale of domestic securities which, in fact, is leading to funds outflow and higher rates, said Thomas Lam Tai Loong, treasury economist at United Overseas Bank.  \par \par \uc2 He said the shorter end of the yield curve is reacting to the MAS action and rising U.S. rates - which have been firming up since the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 The longer-dated bonds may still have support at 3.25%, said one dealer at a local bank, but other analysts said the bearish sentiment for the bond market is far from over.  \par \par \uc2 "For the 10-year Treasurys, our year-end forecast is 5.6%, so we should expect the Singapore bond yield to hit 3.6% by the end of the year," said Simon Klassen, fixed-income research analyst at JP Morgan.  \par \par \uc2 However, an expected rise in yields won't force companies to "to rush to the doors" for more corporate bond issuances because they have already covered themselves last year, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign companies issued S$3.42 billion in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds in 2004, almost double the amount from 2003.  \par \par \uc2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; (65) 6415 4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 10-03-05 0412GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050310e13a0007j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
