\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up Late As Foreign Investment Banks Buy  \b0\par\par\uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 08:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose against its U.S. counterpart late Wednesday in Asia as foreign investment banks bought the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to retest the fresh six-year high of S$1.6180 set late Tuesday in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The yield curve of Singapore government bonds steepened slightly, mimicking the trend of the U.S. Treasurys yield curve late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 At 0645 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6214, down from S$1.6241 late Tuesday. It traded between S$1.6190 and S$1.6225 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 After sliding to S$1.6180 last night, the U.S. dollar immediately came under downward pressure against the local dollar from strong selling by foreign investment houses on behalf of U.S. funds keen to retest that level early in the session, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 A resurgence in concerns over the massive U.S. current account deficit ahead of Friday's U.S. January trade deficit data release prompted overseas speculators to drive the U.S. dollar down as low as S$1.6190 in the morning.  \par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore apparently stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market via a U.K. bank to buy the U.S. dollar around S$1.6190-S$1.6200, pushing the U.S. unit back up to S$1.6220 by midday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Asked about the rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an MAS spokeswoman said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Later in the session, the U.S. dollar consolidated in the S$1.6210-S$1.6220 area, underpinned by speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem any sharp falls of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against its Singaporean counterpart.  \par \par \uc2 In a research report, DBS Bank said Asian central banks of newly industrialized economies will likely seek to temper the upward pressure on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the Korean won, the Taiwan dollar and the Singapore dollar - which have hit multi-year highs against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 From a technical analysis perspective, the U.S. dollar's unexpected sharp drop against the local dollar is picking up momentum and will likely extend lower for the global day, said United Overseas Bank in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 "However, indicators are already oversold and any move below the overnight low of S$1.6180 will likely be limited to the next strong support at S$1.6150," UOB said.  \par \par \uc2 As a short-term trading strategy, UOB recommended selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at S$1.6230 and placing stop-loss orders above S$1.6260, in anticipation of a possible fall to S$1.6150.  \par \par \uc2 Following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest       Previous \par Overnight rate       1.6875%      1.6875% \par Two-year bond yield  2.04%        2.07% \par 10-year bond yield   3.20%        3.17% \par Two-year swap offer  2.34%        2.34% \par 10-year swap offer   3.44%        3.42% \par 2-10-yr swap spread  110 Bps      108 Bps \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; (65) 6415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 09-03-05 0714GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050309e139000ay\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
