\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won pares back gains - rupee up after budget.  \b0\par\par\uc2 764 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2005\par 10:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The South Korean won pared\par early sharp gains on Monday on concerns about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and month-end dollar buying by importers after\par surging on economic data.\par     The won jumped three-quarters of a percent to 1,001 per\par dollar after industrial production for January beat\par expectations and encouraged foreign investors to buy more local\par stocks.\par  \par     The won ended local trading a fifth of a percent higher at\par 1,006 per dollar.\par     The Thai baht gained a quarter of a percent on expectations\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could raise benchmark interest rates on\par Wednesday.\par     The Indian rupee gained a fifth of a percent after the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 finance minister presented the country's budget for 2005/2006,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 cutting corporate taxes and taking steps to boost growth in  \par \par \uc2 infrastructure and rural areas.  \par \par \uc2 The won was lifted earlier on Monday by data which showed  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's factory output rose a faster-than-expected 3.1  \par \par \uc2 percent in January from December.  \par \par \uc2 Signs of a revival in the domestic economy attracted  \par \par \uc2 overseas investors to its stock markets this month, pushing its  \par \par \uc2 benchmark stock index to a five-year high on Monday. Foreign  \par \par \uc2 investors have bought a net 2.32 trillion won in shares so far  \par \par \uc2 this year.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "We see end-March won at 1,000 (per dollar) and end-June at\par 990," said Christy Tan, an analyst at 4CAST Ltd. in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Yet, analysts said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  concerns may keep the won\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from breaching the 1,000 won per dollar barrier in the near  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 term. South Korea could sell more bonds to fund \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to stem the won's rise, Irene Cheung,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 head of Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at ABN AMRO Bank in Singapore,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said in a report.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean data was followed by statistics from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan which showed industrial production rose a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 faster-than-expected 2.1 percent in January from a month  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 earlier.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The two sets of data bolstered expectations that two of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia's biggest economies were reviving from an economic  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 slowdown.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen gained as much as 0.9 percent from late Asian  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 trading on Friday to 104.25 per dollar. The Singapore dollar,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 which closely tracks the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Japan, South Korea and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan, gained a third of a percent to 1.6252/62 per dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Taiwan's markets were closed for a holiday on Monday. South\par Korea's markets are closed on Tuesday.\par     INDIAN BUDGET\par     The rupee gained after Finance Minister Palaniappan\par Chidambaram unveiled a budget that analysts said helped boost\par spending in infrastructure and increase rural income.\par     The budget also cut peak corporate taxes, helping push\par India's benchmark stock index near to a record high.\par     "It's a cautious budget. Some progress has been made in a\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 few areas - such as simplification of the direct taxes and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 lowering the corporate taxes - while carefully remaining  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 within the mandate given by the (coalition) alliance," said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sanjeev Sanyal, economist at Deutsche Bank in Singapore.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Premiums on non-deliverable yuan forwards (NDF) widened  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 after a Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator said the country  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 would gradually increase the amount of yuan that can be  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exchanged under the capital account.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The official said such a move would take the country  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 another step closer towards full convertibility of the yuan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is now convertible for trade purposes.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The premium on the one-year yuan NDF, which investors use  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to bet on any change in the value of the tightly controlled  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rose to price in a 4.6 percent appreciation on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday. The premium has been rising for the past two weeks.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0800 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.53         105.18       +0.62\par  Sing dlr        1.6254         1.6309       +0.34\par  Ko