\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dlr Up Late On Yen Surge;Short-Dated Bonds Down  \b0\par\par\uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2005\par 08:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar climbed late Monday in Asia on a surge in the yen sparked by strong Japanese economic data, though speculation of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on short-dated government bonds rose sharply, leading to curve flattening.  \par \par \uc2 At 0700 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6258, down from S$1.6329 late Friday. It traded between S$1.6256 and S$1.6323 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar kicked off its slide against the local dollar early in the session when the Japanese government said the nation's industrial output rose 2.1% on month in January, better than an average forecast of 1.6% growth by economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires and Nikkei News.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the robust Japanese economic data triggered the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plunge of over half a yen to as low as Y104.50, which in turn dragged the U.S. unit down more than 50 pips to an intraday low of S$1.6253, matching the low set on Feb. 23.  \par \par \uc2 At 0700 GMT, the U.S. unit was at Y104.64, down from Y105.17 Friday in New York.  \par \par \uc2 However, the U.S. dollar's tumble against its Singaporean counterpart was curbed in the session by expectations that the MAS could continue its recent suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts aimed at slowing down the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 'For now, markets will continue to trade around S$1.6250-S$1.6350, although there are some fears of the MAS at the weaker end of the range,' said United Overseas Bank in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 Technical analysis suggests a clear break of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below initial support around S$1.6250, which consists of the lows of Feb. 22-23, would fuel a further U.S. dollar fall toward the six-year low of S$1.6233 set on Jan. 13, then toward the Nov. 20, 1998, low of S$1.6209 in subsequent sessions.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on short-dated Singapore government securities rose late Monday in Asia, as yields on shorter-term U.S. Treasurys climbed Friday and Singapore's short-term interbank rates remained high, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 With the local bond yield curve flattening, some analysts such as JPMorgan and DBS Bank said they prefer to put on flatteners - such as selling the front end and buying the back end - in anticipation of further curve flattening.  \par \par \uc2 DBS Bank, in a research note, said it maintains its 2s/10s flattening strategy.  \par \par \uc2 'Historically, SGS 2s/10s can go as flat as 100 (bps) in a rising rates environment,' DBS Bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                      Latest       Previous \par Overnight rate       2.0000%      2.0000% \par Two-year bond yield  1.99%        1.92% \par 10-year bond yield   3.07%        3.07% \par Two-year swap offer  2.27%        2.19% \par 10-year swap offer   3.30%        3.29% \par 2-10-yr swap spread  103 BPS      110 BPs \par  \par   Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; (65) 6415-4150; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Mary de Wet  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050228e12s005k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
