\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weaker yen and  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  weigh.  \b0\par\par\uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2005\par 05:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Feb 25 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on\par Friday in line with a weakening Japanese yen and on fear of\par heavier \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , causing the\par Korean won and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar to pare some of their steep\par gains this week.\par  \par     The won hovered around 1,008-1,009 per dollar, further away\par from Wednesday's 7-year peak near 998 a dollar.\par     The Singapore dollar was down half a cent from its  highs\par earlier on Friday near 1.6275.\par     The Taiwan dollar fell over a quarter percent at the open\par to hit 31.27 a dollar, but then rallied as Taiwanese stocks hit\par a 10-month peak.\par     Traders said they had heard market talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  the Taiwanese authorities to rein in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Bank   \par \par \uc2  of Korea had not resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, although   \par \par \uc2  the finance ministry said it could issue more bonds to mop up   \par \par \uc2  the won released through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a local Taiwan newspaper reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 central   \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had warned foreign investors against speculating in the   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said short-term factors such as the focus   \par \par \uc2  on yields, which was undermining the yen, and the worry of   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would weigh on the regionals, despite the longer   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "With the focus on yield, Asia is obviously not the\par favourite," said Bhanu Baweja, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS.\par     Baweja said the decline in the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  provided\par an opportunity for investors to establish fresh long positions.\par     He said he would pick the Taiwan dollar, Sing dollar,\par Indian rupee  and Thai baht, although he would wait for\par the currently high volatility levels to drop.\par     Even the rise in crude oil prices to more than $50 a barrel\par was overshadowed by other factors for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par oil-importing Asian markets.\par     These included a boost for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  early this week\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par when a Korean document outlining plans to diversify foreign\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserves sparked a dollar sell off. Asian authorities have\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since assured markets they are not selling the dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par COORDINATED \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But markets continued to speculate on what could have been\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par discussed at a closed-door meeting of Asian policy makers in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bangkok on Tuesday.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par According to a Korean newspaper report, the meeting was\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par held to discuss how to cope with a weak U.S. dollar and the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possibility of a Chinese yuan revaluation.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Policy makers from South Korea, Japan, China and the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10-member Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) met in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bangkok. Japanese officials said there was no discussion on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par halting the dollar's slide, and the group merely exchanged\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par views on macroeconomic issues.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said speculation about the meeting was no longer\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par having an impact on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , although the won's 2 percent\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise earlier this week had markets assuming that the policy\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par makers might have decided to accommodate some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strength.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Are they thinking about coordinated appreciation of Asian\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so that there is appreciation against the dollar but\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not a massive trade-weighted appreciation for any particular\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ?" Baweja said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "That was not clear. It remains completely speculative.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a balance of payments flows basis\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are massively undervalued and need to appreciate."\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.40         104.67       -0.69\par  Sing dlr        1.6325         1.6260       -0.40\par  Taiwan dlr      31.178         31.175       -0.01\par  Korean won     1008.80        1006.40       -0.24\par  Baht             38.42          38.37       -0.13\par  Peso             54.68          54.76       +0.15\par  Rupiah         9262.00        9230.00       -0.35\par  Rupee            43.68          43.67       -0.02\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.40         102.45       -2.80\par  Sing dlr        1.6325         1.6310       -0.09\par  Taiwan dlr      31.178         31.917       +2.37\par  Korean won     1008.80        1035.10       +2.61\par  Baht             38.42          38.85       +1.12\par  Peso             54.68          56.28       +2.93\par  Rupiah         9262.00        9270.00       +0.09\par  Rupee            43.68          43.47       -0.48.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050225e12p002jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
