\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  fear weighs on won, Taiwan dlr.  \b0\par\par\uc2 720 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2005\par 09:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Feb 24 (Reuters) - The Korean won and the Taiwan\par dollar were pulled off intra-day highs on Thursday by talk of\par dollar-buying by the authorities, but markets remained bullish\par on the two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after their run-up earlier in the week.\par     The won hit a seven-year peak of 998 a dollar on Wednesday\par after a Bank of Korea document referring to diversification of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves sparked a dollar sell-off against\par major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     A Korean media report suggesting Asian policy makers met in\par Bangkok on Tuesday to discuss their approach to the dollar's\par weakness also boosted the regionals.\par     Traders said speculation the policy makers might have\par agreed to accommodate some strength in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had\par underpinned the regionals.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     And, although the Korean authorities were suspected of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier this week, their failure to stop a 2\par percent rally from 1,024 to levels above 1,000 won a dollar had\par intensified the dollar selling, traders added.\par  \par     But at 0740 GMT on Thursday, the won had slipped to 1,006 a\par dollar, down a quarter percent from the morning's levels.\par     The Taiwan dollar fell to 31.17 a dollar from a 4-=   year\par peak of 31.09 it struck in morning deals.\par     Traders suspected the Korean authorities might have mopped\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 up around $200 million in the morning to cap the won, alongside  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 heavy verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The Korean finance minister said the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 won's gains were temporary and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Park Seung  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said the won might decline around April.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think we will not see any bouts of outperformance in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for a few days. They will move sideways for a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 while," said John Cairns, head of research at IDEAglobal.com.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Japanese finance ministry official said on Thursday there  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 had been no discussion of trying to halt the dollar's decline  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at the Bangkok meeting.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     At their highs, the won had risen 2 percent since Monday\par and the Taiwan dollar had risen 1.4 percent.\par     The Singapore dollar also slipped slightly on Thursday\par after its one percent rise since Monday.\par     The Philippine peso and Indonesian rupiah held steady.\par     Referring to remarks by authorities in Taiwan, Korea and\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan playing down the idea of reserves diversification, JP  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Morgan strategist Claudio Piron said the regional central banks  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 were clearly sensitive to sentiment on the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Policy makers will not, through their own actions,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exacerbate U.S. dollar losses. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stability or gradual  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation remains the dominant policy mandate and it serves  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 no interest for policymakers to accelerate dollar losses,"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Piron said in a note.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "In this context, any effort to diversify reserves will not\par be designed as a destabilising influence on the dollar."\par     YEN-WON CROSS\par     Meanwhile, the yen rallied during Asian trading, shrugging\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 off Wednesday's release of the minutes of a U.S. Federal  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve meeting, which reiterated the Fed's commitment to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 raising rates at a measured pace.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The yen came off a 4-=   year low against the won. It\par rallied to 9.6 won per yen, off overnight levels of 9.54.\par     The yen has stayed below the 10 won level most of this\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 month, defying market belief that the Korean authorities would  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively at that level to keep the won  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 competitive versus the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0804 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.67         104.70       +0.03\par  Sing dlr        1.6260         1.6293       +0.20\par  Taiwan dlr      31.175         31.190       +0.05\par  Korean won     1006.40        1003.90       -0.25\par  Baht             38.37          38.34       -0.07\par  Peso             54.76          54.67       -0.17\par  Rupiah         9230.00        9245.00       +0.16\par  Rupee            43.69          43.71       +0.05\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.67         102.45       -2.12\par  Sing dlr        1.6260         1.6310       +0.31\par  Taiwan dlr      31.175         31.917       +2.38\par  Korean won     1006.40        1035.10       +2.85\par  Baht             38.37          38.85       +1.26\par  Peso             54.76          56.28       +2.78\par  Rupiah         9230.00        9270.00       +0.43\par  Rupee            43.69          43.47       -0.50.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050224e12o007hj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
