\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ ASIA DEBT: Singapore IRS Debate: To Steepen Or Flatten?  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Shen Hong  \par \uc2 1,031 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2005\par 01:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires Column  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Not long ago, the dominant theme in Singapore's fixed-income market was that interest-rate curves here would follow those in the U.S. by flattening.  \par \par \uc2 Some strategists and traders insist the island city-state's bond yields and interest rate swaps are bound to mimic the months-long flattening trend seen in U.S. Treasurys and IRS. But now, even before the steep Singapore curves have had a chance to flatten, others are arguing that there's room for the gap of long-term over short-term yields and IRS rates to widen further.  \par \par \uc2 Proponents of flattening, such as DBS Bank, say persistently strong appetite for local fixed-income assets and tamedinflation don't warrant sharply higher long-term interest rates here, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to support short-term rates with a tight bias in monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 But those in the steepening camp are this week citing fast-rising long U.S. Treasury yields and talk of a bulging local bond pipeline to argue that the long end of the Singapore interest rate curves should gather upward momentum, pushing short and long rates even farther apart.  \par \par \uc2 Since talk began at the start of the year of an impending flattening here, the spread of the 10-year Singapore dollar IRS swap over the two-year rate has instead widened 15 basis points to 114 basis points. The similar spread on Singapore government bond yields has also widened 15 basis points, to 118 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 During the same period, the U.S. interest rate curves have flattened rapidly, with the IRS 2-10-year spread shrinking by 32 basis points to around 83.7 basis points. Playing for a similar flattening in the U.S. Treasurys curve has been a major trade in that market since last year, despite the Federal Reserve's steady diet of interest rate rises at the short end.  \par \par \uc2 The phenomenon has become pronounced enough for Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan last week to brand it a 'conundrum,' sparking a sharp rebound of U.S. long yields as traders and investors wondered whether the one-way flattening ride was over.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore, despite predictions of a flattening, has been decoupled from U.S. curve moves this year largely because of the Fed's inexorable tightening, which contrasts with an outlook for slower growth in the island republic. The 2-10-year spread in Singapore has widened a further 4 basis points in the past week, fueled by talk that a company was preparing to issue a long-dated Singapore-dollar bond as soon as this week.  \par \par \uc2 'We heard the new issue size could be pretty big,' said a trader at a Singapore bank. 'If the market doesn't have the appetite for it, the curve could steepen further.'  \par \par \uc2 In addition, the post-Greenspan steepening in the U.S. Treasury curve has begun spilling over into the Singapore market.  \par \par \uc2 While the market has so far responded calmly to an unexpectedly large S$1.2 billion reopening Thursday of a 10-year government bond, uncertainty will likely linger until the bond's auction Thursday. The market had mostly expected the reopened issue to be worth S$800 million to S$1 billion. If demand for the bond is weak, paying interest may increase at the long end of the IRS curve, pushing swap rates up.  \par \par \uc2 But despite such upward risks for long-dated rates, some strategists are standing by their curve flatteners.  \par \par \uc2 DBS recommends investors sell the two-year bond and buy the 10-year, targeting a flattening 100 basis points in one to three months.  \par \par \uc2 Historically, the yield-curve spread can narrow only to 100 basis points 'in a rising-rate environment,' says DBS strategist Chia Woon Khien. 'Unless the current hiking cycle is coming to a halt, there's no reason to disrupt the flattening strategy, especially in U.S. Treasurys, which have more scope for further flattening.'  \par \par \uc2 Chia said the IRS curve will behave in a broadly similar fashion but that she sees more room for the bond-yield curve to flatten. Indeed, DBS recommends a widener on the 10-year bond-swap spread.  \par \par \uc2 She is also adamant that long rates in Singapore will remain in check thanks to yield-hungry investors, as inflation stays benign and the local economy transforms itself to a productivity-oriented nature from an investment-driven one in past decades. 'On an asset-allocation basis, you look at nominal growth, which is no longer like the go-go days,' Chia said. 'People would still want to seek relatively more comfort in bonds than equities.'  \par \par \uc2 The debate over the Singapore rate curves also hinges on the outlook for monetary policy here, with the flattener camp expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to maintain its tightening bias at its next policy meeting in April but steepener fans looking for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease.  \par \par \uc2 'We deem the chance next to nil,' Chia said, adding that the government's new pro-growth budget would offset some of the current weakness in exports. 'Besides, the MAS's tenet is that the Singapore dollar policy is to defend inflation, not exports.'  \par \par \uc2 The MAS uses the Singapore dollar exchange rate rather than interest rates as monetary policy tool for this small, trade-dominated economy. But when the authority \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the resulting drain of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar liquidity from the interbank market puts upward pressure on short-term rates.  \par \par \uc2 In the midst of this heated debate, some traders say both arguments may in fact prove right and that it's best to stay flexible - anticipating a steepening for the next week or two due to the bond-supply pressures, then reverting to a longer-term flattener trade after long rates stabilize.  \par \par \uc2 The 2-10 IRS spread has an immediate upside of 125 basis points, where investors could consider taking profits and entering a flattener with a target of 100 basis points, traders say.  \par \par \uc2 -By Shen Hong, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4032; hong.shen@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by William Mallard  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050223e12n000gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
