\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Trapped in ranges by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  concerns.  \b0\par\par\uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2005\par 05:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Feb 21 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par trapped in narrow ranges on Monday, with robust foreign\par investment inflows into their stock markets offset by concern\par about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the weakness of the yen.\par     The yen was down nearly half a percent from Friday after\par last week's weak economic data and on waning expectations of\par any immediate change in China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime.\par  \par     The Korean won was little changed from Friday, trading\par around 1,023 per dollar, close to last week's seven-year highs.\par     The Taiwan dollar hugged levels around 31.52 a dollar, held\par back from four-year highs beyond 31.50 by talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily to cap the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week.\par     Foreign portfolio investment inflows are putting upward\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2  pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Foreigners have bought close to T$100   \par \par \uc2  billion of Taiwan shares since late January and the market is   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai baht was in a 38.53-38.58 range, while the Sing\par dollar was on the firmer side of 1.64 a dollar.\par     Analysts said Thailand had received over $1 billion of\par foreign portfolio investments so far in 2005, more than in any\par year from 2001 to 2004.\par     "The big theme at the moment is whether or not dollar\par weakness is going to resume," said John Cairns, head of\par research at IDEAglobal.com.\par     "The more the dollar stays here, the more people are going\par to be worried about their long Asia positions," he said.\par     There was also the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par rein in the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he said.\par     Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week, Thailand's reserves data showed heavy dollar-buying\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interention and in South Korea the renewed heavy issuance of\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary stabilisation bonds suggested possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cairns said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The moves in Hong Kong forwards and Taiwan dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forwards also confirmed speculators were\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trimming their Asian positions, he added.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even the Philippine peso which has the benefit of high\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yields and has been boosted this year by foreign investment\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flows, ceded ground to the dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It hit 54.66 in early deals but soon fell to 54.81 a dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on worries that a proposal to introduce a value-added-tax\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par system might be diluted or rejected by legislators.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 