\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dlr Down Late; Weak Yen, Rumored MAS Rate Check  \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2005\par 08:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar edged lower against its U.S. counterpart in Asia Wednesday on broad-based yen weakness and on speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was checking on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were nearly flat ahead of Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's two-day semiannual congressional testimony that begins later in the global day.  \par \par \uc2 At 0640, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6414, above S$1.6412 late Tuesday. It traded between S$1.6374 and S$1.6419 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  kicked off the Asian session on a positive note against the local dollar as interbank players bought U.S. dollars on rumors that the MAS had called several banks about the U.S. dollar-Singapore dollar pair when the U.S. unit was trading around S$1.6380, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Concerns that \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. dollar against the local dollar spurred the interbank-led short-covering that helped to boost the U.S. unit as high as S$1.6419 in the afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's slide against major rivals throughout most of the session also contributed to the U.S. dollar's climb against its Singapore counterpart, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Early in the session, the Japanese government said Japan's real gross domestic product shrank 0.1% in the October-December period from the previous quarter, undershooting economists' expectations for GDP growth of 0.1%. The government also lowered previous GDP figures to a 0.3% decline in the July-September period and a 0.2% fall in the April-June period.  \par \par \uc2 'Technically, Japan is in a recession,' said a local dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The technical definition of a recession is at least two consecutive quarters of economic contraction.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar continued to trade firmly in the low-S$1.6400s later in the session, though its upside was capped by rumored offers from a U.K. bank in the S$1.6410-S$1.6415 area, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                      Latest   Previous \par Overnight rate       1.5000%  1.6250% \par Two-year bond yield  1.77%    1.76% \par 10-year bond yield   2.91%    2.90% \par Two-year swap offer  2.03%    2.03% \par 10-year swap offer   3.13%    3.14% \par 2-10-yr swap spread  110 BPs  111 BPs \par  \par   Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Singapore Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4150;djnews.singapore.bureaudowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Mary de Wet  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050216e12g004v2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
