\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won slips, Sing dollar softer.  \b0\par\par\uc2 881 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2005\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 11 (Reuters) - The South Korean won fell and\par most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were soft on Friday after the Japanese\par yen's decline overnight and North Korea's declaration that it\par had nuclear weapons.\par     The Japanese yen's recovery in later trades helped some of\par the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recoup, leaving only the won and the\par Sing dollar down over a quarter percent since they were last\par traded earlier in the week.\par    The Philippine peso was steadier around 54.80 per dollar,\par having come off its highest levels in over a year earlier this\par week.\par     Japanese markets were closed on Friday. Other regional\par markets in Taiwan and Hong Kong also remained shut for extended\par Lunar New Year holidays, exaggerating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves.\par     The won fell in early deals as trading resumed after the\par festival holidays. It hit 1,038 per dollar, down from Monday's\par levels near 1,029.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     North Korea declared on Thursday for the first time that it\par possessed nuclear weapons, and it pulled out indefinitely from\par six-nation talks on its atomic ambitions, saying it needed a\par defense against a hostile United States.\par  \par     Korean stocks fell, paring some of the rapid gains the\par index has made in the past month.\par     Traders played down the impact of the North Korean\par statement on markets and attributed the won's decline more to\par the Japanese yen.\par     "While all three rating agencies have listed the North\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korean issue as an impediment to a ratings upgrade, only  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's has adjusted the ratings in response to developments in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the nuclear issue," Dominique Dwor-Frecaut of Barclays Capital  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 wrote in a note to clients.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and equity market weakness has been attributed to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 North Korea's latest announcement, but we expect this to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 subside since, as explained above, we do not see any lasting  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 significant consequences from this statement," she said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 James Malcolm, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with Deutsche Bank,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said the yen's cross rate against the won showed the won was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 not badly hit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Yen/Korea is still below 9.8. The market is not taking it  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (the North Korea declaration) terribly seriously," said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malcolm.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen was off its three-month low of 106.86 against the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar after U.S. data showed the country's trade deficit hit a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 record $617.7 billion last year. But it had shed nearly 3  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent during the week after upbeat comments by Federal  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on the U.S. current account  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deficit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won was quoted at 9.78 per yen, near its overnight  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 levels of 9.70, which were the highest in over 2 years. It has  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 remained stronger than 10 per yen this month, a level markets  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 believe Korean authorities and businesses are sensitive to when  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 evaluating the won's competitiveness in export markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Deutsche's Malcolm said markets had become less responsive  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over time to North Korea's threats and declarations of nuclear  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ambitions.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     He cited an instance in late 2003, when the won fell beyond\par 11 per yen.\par     "It is so difficult to gauge that kind of tail risk. Over\par time the reaction becomes smaller and smaller.\par     "I don't see it being a major factor at the moment,"\par Malcolm said, referring to the North Korea news.\par     Markets were becoming increasingly bullish on South Korea,\par he noted, citing reports of improving retail sales and the\par surge in stocks to five-year highs on Monday.\par     SING DOLLAR - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ?\par     Elsewhere, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar recovered from two-month\par lows near 1.66 reached late on Thursday in offshore trading.\par But it stayed on the weaker side of 1.65 a dollar.\par     Economists at UBS said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to contain volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The MAS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 manages the Sing dollar within a trade-weighted basket of  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its trading partners.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As per UBS estimates, the Sing dollar trade-weighted index  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 or nominal effective exchange rate (NEER) was now 0.5 percent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 below the mid-point of that secret band, compared with 0.5  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent above the mid-point around January 19.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The MAS not only manages the level of the NEER but also\par the volatility within the band," UBS said.\par     "As such the risk of MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy Sing dollar\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 has increased even though the Sing dollar NEER is still well  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 within the plus/minus 2 percent trading range around the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mid-point," UBS said.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0836 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.56         105.83       +0.26\par  Sing dlr        1.6513         1.6475       -0.23\par  Korean won     1033.20        1029.00       -0.41\par  Baht             38.56          38.52       -0.12\par  Peso             54.75          54.65       -0.18\par  Rupiah         9268.00        9280.00       +0.13\par  Rupee            43.80          43.78       -0.03\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.56         102.45       -2.95\par  Sing dlr        1.6513         1.6310       -1.23\par  Korean won     1033.20        1035.10       +0.18\par  Baht             38.56          38.85       +0.75\par  Peso             54.75          56.28       +2.79\par  Rupiah         9268.00        9270.00       +0.02\par  Rupee            43.80          43.47       -0.74.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050211e12b008kh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
