\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht, peso gain - won dips on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2005\par 09:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Feb 4 (Reuters) - The Thai baht and Philippine\par peso gained on Friday as traders bid up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  likely to\par outperform in Asia in coming months as they benefit from\par growing economies and foreign inflows into their stock markets.\par     But the South Korean won weakened on worries the Bank of\par Korea may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb its strength, particularly against\par the yen, to keep exports competitive.\par     The baht rose half a percent to 38.33 per dollar. The\par Philippine peso -- the best-performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia this\par year after being the second-worst performer in 2004 -- rose 0.4\par percent to a 15-month high of 54.67 per dollar.\par     The Philippines and Thailand both expect their economies to\par grow about 6 percent this year. The booming stock markets in\par both countries got a further boost this week when Calpers, the\par U.S. pension fund, decided to include Thailand and retain the\par Philippines in the list of countries where it plans to invest.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It's clear that people are looking for some yields and are\par willing to take Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risks and look at the other\par catch-up candidates such as the peso," said David Simmonds,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland in Singapore.\par     The peso has been helped in the past month by sustained\par foreign investment in the country's stock and bond markets and\par by signs the government is taking steps to boost its tax\par revenue to reduce the fiscal deficit.\par  \par     The Philippines' benchmark stock index surged to a\par five-year high this week and traded near that level on Friday.\par     ABN AMRO said in a report that the baht, Asia's second-best\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 performer this year, could rise after a general election this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weekend that Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra's ruling Thai  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rak Thai party seems certain to win.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The bank expects the baht to strengthen to 37.8 per dollar\par by the end of the first quarter.\par     The Indonesian rupiah gained a fifth of a percent to 9,195\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 per dollar on expectations the government would cut fuel  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 subsidies. They contributed to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's underperformance  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 last year because of worries about the government budget  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deficit.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's Planning Minister Sri Mulyani said on Thursday  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the government may raise domestic fuel product prices by an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 average 30 percent before the end of March.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ?  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won lost a fifth of a percent to 1,026.6 per dollar. It  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 also weakened to about 9.82 per yen from a 1-1/2-year high of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 about 9.78 per yen on Thursday. The won has surged 6.5 percent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against the yen in the past three months.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The won's move has been too far, too fast," Simmonds said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I suspect we're close to stepped-up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again by the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korean authorities."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     South Korean Finance Minister Lee Hun-jai said rising U.S.\par interest rates would help stabilise the won against the dollar.\par     While South Korea has reduced the size of a planned bond\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sale, geared to raising \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  funds, the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 authorities would still sell the won if it strengthened beyond  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 9.80 per yen, Simmonds said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee fell as much as a quarter of a percent to 43.53,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weakening from a five-year high on Thursday, on concern the  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would act against further appreciation.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Deutsche Bank said on Thursday that one of the most\par attractive trading opportunities in Asia was to sell the rupee\par for other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the Taiwan dollar     A\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government decision on Thursday to raise interest rate paid by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Employees Provident Fund by one percentage point could add  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to the government subsidies and fiscal deficit, Michael  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spencer, Deutche's chief economist for Asia, said in a report.   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at   0801 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.48         104.15       -0.32\par  Sing dlr        1.63