\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yuan talk,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worry limit moves.  \b0\par\par\uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2005\par 10:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Jan 28 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were trapped\par in tight ranges on Friday, with the Korean won pushed to a\par 7-year high, caught between fresh speculation of an imminent\par Chinese yuan revaluation and the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Philippine peso bounced off a one-year high of 55.03 a\par dollar, the Taiwan dollar was capped at 31.77 a dollar, and the\par Singapore dollar was almost a cent off an overnight peak of\par 1.6280.\par     The initial rally was spurred by comments from Yu Yongding,\par a Chinese economist and member of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary\par policy committee, who told a seminar at the World Economic\par Forum in Davos it was time China made the yuan more flexible.\par     But the yen and other regionals fell after a Dow Jones\par report quoted a Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official as saying Yu's\par comments were not an official view. Separately, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reiterated its policy of keeping the yuan stable.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Worries about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of next week's Group of\par Seven meeting also weighed on the regionals. As well, the\par dollar was supported ahead of U.S. jobs and GDP data and a\par Federal Reserve policy meeting next week.\par     Analysts said they expected more comments from Chinese\par officials in coming days, aimed at toning down market\par speculation ahead of the G7 meeting on Feb. 4 and 5. China,\par India and other emerging economies have been invited to talks\par with G7 officials.\par     "We believe that the Chinese authorities are keen to\par maintain some semblance of two-way risk in the market in\par preparation of when they do gradually introduce greater\par flexibility," UBS said in a note.\par     "As such, it would not be surprising to see official\par comments over the coming days that emphasise that a stronger\par yuan does not automatically follow a move to greater\par flexibility."\par     Chinese yuan offshore non-deliverable forwards were\par unaffected by the swings in the yen, and priced in a higher\par premium on the yuan. Yuan NDFs were dealt at 4,150 points\par premium for one-year yuan, pricing in 5.3 percent gains.\par     Yu's comments came near the end of a volatile week for yuan\par forwards and regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , driven by comments from U.S.,\par European and Chinese officials for and against a yuan shift.\par     Speculation China would free up the pegged yuan fed through\par to the Malaysian ringgit. One-year ringgit NDFs were quoted at\par 3.695 per dollar, stronger than the peg level at 3.8.\par     WON RISES\par     The Korean won rose to a fresh seven-year peak near 1,023 a\par dollar, continuing to receive support from the view that it\par would be boosted by turbulence in the bond markets caused by\par worries over issuance.\par     That stems from the view the Bank of Korea would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par less to buy dollars if their capacity to issue bonds to offset\par that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was reduced.\par     But David Simmonds, markets strategist with Royal Bank of\par Scotland, said recent measures by Korean authorities did not\par mean the risks of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were lower.\par     The won, Asia's best performer in 2004, was at its highest\par since late 2000 in trade-weighted terms, Simmonds said. He said\par the won would not outperform its trading partners but would\par gradually move up to 1,000 per dollar in coming months.\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \par  Change on the day at   0817 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.16         103.06       -0.10\par  Sing dlr        1.6358         1.6323       -0.21\par  Taiwan dlr      31.802         31.863       +0.19\par  Korean won     1023.50        1028.00       +0.44\par  Baht             38.45          38.51       +0.16\par  Peso             55.09          55.11       +0.04\par  Rupiah         9144.00        9140.00       -0.04\par  Rupee            43.77          43.78       +0.03\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.16         102.45       -0.69\par  Sing dlr        1.6358         1.6310       -0.29\par  Taiwan dlr      31.802         31.917       +0.36\par  Korean won     1023.50        1035.10       +1.13\par  Baht             38.45          38.85       +1.04\par  Peso             55.09          56.28       +2.16\par  Rupiah         9144.00        9270.00       +1.38\par  Rupee            43.77          43.47       -0.67.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050128e11s0093z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
