\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Dn Late Amid Concerns MAS Might  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2005\par 08:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar edged lower against its U.S. counterpart in Asia late Tuesday, pressured by speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a sharp slide of the U.S. unit.  \par \par \uc2 The yield curve for Singapore government bonds flattened slightly, in tandem with Monday's flattening of the U.S. Treasurys yield curve, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0645 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6341, slightly up from S$1.6326 late in Asia Monday. It traded between S$1.6318 and S$1.6349 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 After rising as high as S$1.6345 on broad-based U.S. dollar strength early in the session, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon came under downward pressure from various players looking to rebuild short positions against the local dollar ahead of major upcoming events such as the weekend elections in Iraq.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was also dragged lower against the Singapore unit by speculator-led selling of euros for Singapore dollars after European policy-makers continued to make veiled calls on Asian countries to adopt a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate stance.  \par \par \uc2 Late Monday, French Finance Minister Herve Gaymard said the Feb. 4-5 meeting of G-7 finance ministers will provide a necessary forum for commitments to correct fluctuations in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.  \par \par \uc2 "In Europe we're aware of the need to boost the growth potential, while the U.S. is well aware of the need to act on its deficit and Asia is conscious of a need for more flexibility," Gaymard said at a Franco-German summit of ministers and central bankers.  \par \par \uc2 Although the U.S. dollar fell as low as S$1.6318 at midday, it later rebounded to as high as S$1.6349 on mild short-covering spurred by speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a sharp slide of the U.S. unit below the psychologically important S$1.6300 level, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 While the overall outlook for the U.S. dollar against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still appears weak, based on technical analysis, the downward momentum isn't strong and the solid support at S$1.6275 will likely hold for the global day, said United Overseas Bank in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 "In other words, expect another down-move but this should be followed by a rebound later on," UOB said.  \par \par \uc2 As a short-term trading plan, UOB recommends buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at S$1.6300 and placing stop-loss orders below S$1.6275, in anticipation of a rise to S$1.6360.  \par \par \uc2 Following are the overnight interbank rate, yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest   Previous \par Overnight rate       1.5625%  1.4375% \par Two-year bond yield  1.68%    1.64% \par 10-year bond yield   2.88%    2.88% \par Two-year swap offer  1.93%    1.92% \par 10-year swap offer   3.09%    3.08% \par 2-10-yr swap spread  116 BPs  116 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2