\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Down on yen,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2005\par 09:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Jan 14 (Reuters) - Despite the renewed pressure\par from western policy makers for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rise, the\par regionals fell on Friday owing to a weaker Japanese yen and the\par fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        suffered the heaviest losses,\par retreating nearly 2 cents from a fresh six-year peak of 1.6235\par struck overnight on talk that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through local banks.\par     The Korean won                   fell over half a percent,\par coming off an offshore 7-year high of 1,032.7, as the yen too\par ceded some ground to the dollar despite gaining against the\par euro.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        was also a loser, pushed below\par Thursday's one-month high by scepticism over the benefits of\par debt relief granted by the Paris Club of creditors.\par     The U.S.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar rallied against the euro overnight after\par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said the\par consensus within the Group of Seven nations was for an orderly\par appreciation in Asian emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Bank of Canada Senior Deputy Governor Paul Jenkins and New\par York Fed President Timothy Geithner also urged exchange rate\par flexibility in Asia.\par     Ahead of a G7 meeting in the first week of February, many\par analysts were expecting further rhetoric for Asia to take up\par its share of a broad dollar downtrend, aimed at helping correct\par a record U.S. trade deficit.\par     Ray Farris, markets strategist with CSFB, said there was\par little to suggest that the United States would make any major\par statements on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the G7 and that U.S.\par authorities appeared to prefer markets to determine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par levels.\par  \par     Still, he said, "There may very well be some G7-related\par pressure on Asia."\par     "It is unlikely that China will alter its exchange rate\par regime simply because of criticism or pressure from G7," Farris\par said.\par     Economists at UBS also said that the Asian authorities\par would now begin to fret about further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains.\par     "The end game for the U.S. dollar does indeed require the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar to fall more against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in order to help  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the greenback fall on a broad trade-weighted basis," UBS said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in a note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But we are not convinced that Asian policy makers are  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 willing at this stage to tolerate much stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 here, any more than they were following last February's G7."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUPIAH RETREATS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupiah's decline did not surprise many analysts. It  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 comes after a 2.4 percent rise in a week, driven by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expectations of aid inflows after the tsunami and the debt  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 moratorium.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The club agreed to an initial three-month debt moratorium  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for th countries hit by the disaster and said it could be  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 extended.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Indonesian chief economics minister Aburizal Bakrie said it\par would be good if the country got a year's moratorium.\par     JP Morgan's strategist Caludio Piron said in a note the\par risk was that only the immediate three-month relief would\par materialize.\par     "While near-term sentiment could drive further rupiah\par gains, the eventual agreement is not expected to turn\par underlying balance of payments trends," he said.\par     "The potential debt relief compares unfavorably to the $21\par billion of private and public external debt servicing due for\par the country this year," he said.\par     Citigroup's strategist Cliff Tan said the rupiah might have\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over-reacted to the debt relief plans, given that Indonesia was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 getting only some time to pay its debt, not money. Also,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rebuilding the tsunami-struck areas would require future  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 imports, Tan said.   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at   0836 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       102.87         102.31       -0.54\par  Sing dlr        1.6406         1.6273       -0.81\par  Taiwan dlr      32.019         31.868       -0.47\par  Korean won     1042.70        1036.60       -0.59\par  Baht             38.75          38.76       +0.03\par  Peso             55.64          55.67       +0.05\par  Rupiah         9160.00        91