\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Under pressure to rise, rupiah retreats.  \b0\par\par\uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2005\par 04:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 14 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mixed\par on Friday, under renewed pressure from western policy makers to\par rise but with gains thwarted by market fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar and the Indonesian rupiah were early\par losers, the former retreating a cent from a fresh 6-year peak\par of 1.6235 struck overnight on concern the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sap some strength from the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The rupiah was below Thursday's one-month high, pressured\par by scepticism over the benefits of debt relief granted by the\par Paris Club of creditors.\par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held on to marginal gains, with the\par Korean won close to an offshore 7-year high of 1,032.7, aided\par by a firmer yen against the euro and a barrage of statements.\par     The U.S.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar rallied against the euro overnight after\par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said the\par consensus within the Group of Seven nations was for an orderly\par appreciation in Asian emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Bank of Canada Senior Deputy Governor Paul Jenkins and New\par York Fed President Timothy Geithner also urged exchange rate\par flexibility in Asia.\par     Ahead of a G7 meeting in the first week of February, many\par analysts were expecting further rhetoric for Asia to take up\par its share of a broad dollar downtrend, aimed at helping correct\par a record U.S. trade deficit.\par     Ray Farris, markets strategist with CSFB, said there was\par little to suggest that the United States would make any major\par statements on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the G7 and that U.S.\par authorities appeared to prefer markets to determine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par levels.\par  \par     Still, he said, "There may very well be some G7-related\par pressure on Asia."\par     "It is unlikely that China will alter its exchange rate\par regime simply because of criticism or pressure from G7," Farris\par said.\par     YUAN PREMIUM RISES\par     Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards have moved this week\par to price in a higher premium as China faced renewed calls to\par relax its yuan policy and after recent data.\par     The U.S. dollar's downtrend resumed this week after\par November's trade data. China reported that its trade surplus\par increased to its highest in 9 years in December.\par     "There is a rising likelihood that non-Japan Asia, notably\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China, will be pressured to share the burden of U.S. dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 realignment in the G7 meeting on 4-5 Feb," Irene Cheung of ABN  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AMRO Bank said in a note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We expect dollar/yuan NDFs to come under downward pressure  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on speculation that China might give in to external pressure.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, we continue to see a low probability of a yuan change  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in the near term."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One-year NDFs were quoted at 4,300 points, pricing in a 5.5  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent appreciation in the yuan. The yuan is effectively  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pegged around 8.28 per U.S. dollar.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WORRY  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Farris said the won was the only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia which had  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strengthened significantly in trade-weighted terms. Even the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sing dollar was within the trade-weighted band authorities  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 manage it in, despite being nominally near 6-year highs.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Farris also expected further dollar weakness against the\par yen, and for Asia to lag the yen's appreciation.\par     Economists at UBS also said that the Asian authorities\par would now begin to fret about further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains.\par     "The end game for the U.S. dollar does indeed require the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar to fall more against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in order to help  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the greenback fall on a broad trade-weighted basis," UBS said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in a note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But we are not convinced that Asian policymakers are  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 willing at this stage to tolerate much stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 here, any more than they were following last February's G7."  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0238 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       102.78         1